    "fia_entry_exit_rules": "15.1 In accordance with Chapter 4, Articles 4 and 6 of Appendix L to the ISC drivers must\nfollow the procedures at pit entry and pit exit.\n15.2 Pertaining to Chapter 4, Article 4 of Appendix L to the ISC any driver passing to the left\nhand side of the pit entry after the safety car line 1 will be considered as entering the pit lane.\n15.3 For safety reasons, drivers must keep to the left of the solid white line at the pit entry when they\nare entering the pits\n15.4 Additionally, drivers must keep to the left of the 1st bollard and to the right of the 2nd bollard\nat the pit entry road.\n15.5 During the reconnaissance laps prior to the Sprint and the Race drivers are allowed to cross\nthe white line separating the pit exit road from the circuit.\n15.6 For the safe and orderly conduct of the event, during any live session, team personnel are\nnot allowed in the pit lane beyond the white line crossing the pit lane near pit entry, as\nindicated in the picture below.\n15.7 A marshal placed at the end of the pit exit road (after the practice start area) will display a\nblue flag for the cars leaving pit lane when another car is approaching on the track.\n15.8 Light panel PE located before the pit entry road on the Left Hand side is only to signal any\nincident at the pit entry road using the yellow, double yellow or the white signals.",
